<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Abraham on John, Complected</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/abraham/</link><description>Recent content in Abraham on John, Complected</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2026</copyright><lastBuildDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://john-nicholson.github.io/tags/abraham/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Remember Who You Are — Remember Whose You Are</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-remember-whose-you-are/</link><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-remember-whose-you-are/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Romans&amp;#43;4%3A16%E2%80%9321&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Romans 4:16–21&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt; and &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Galatians&amp;#43;3%3A26%E2%80%9329&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Galatians 3:26–29&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;105%3A1%E2%80%9311&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 105:1–11&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There are moments when it helps to remember not only &lt;strong&gt;who we are&lt;/strong&gt;, but &lt;strong&gt;whose we are&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Life changes. Our strength changes. Our responsibilities change. Sometimes even the way we see ourselves can change. But if you belong to Jesus, there is something deeper than all of that.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You belong to God.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You are part of his family. You are part of a story that began long before you were born and will continue long after your own lifetime.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Remember Who You Are — I Have Called You by Name</title><link>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-i-have-called-you-by-name/</link><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://john-nicholson.github.io/devotionals/remember-who-you-are-i-have-called-you-by-name/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis&amp;#43;12%3A1%E2%80%934&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Genesis 12:1–4&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt; and &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis&amp;#43;17%3A1%E2%80%937&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Genesis 17:1–7&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;139%3A1%E2%80%9318&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 139:1–18&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;There can be something unsettling about feeling less certain of yourself than you once did. Names can become harder to remember. Familiar things can sometimes feel unfamiliar. Even our own story can become more difficult to hold together.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But God does not know us in the uncertain way that we sometimes know ourselves. &lt;strong&gt;He knows us completely.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>